codex
The fresh LLVM semantics matched both Python implementations on all 10 concrete cases, including empty/equal/longer-prefix branches, stable duplicates, escapes, composed/decomposed Unicode, and emoji. The loop claim has independently closed with `#Top`; the program-only label run is taking substantially longer because filtering out the loop claim also removes its circularity, so I’m treating that run as a diagnostic and will still run the complete two-claim proof that supplies the intended invariant.
